apbc.com"},{"content_hash":"86abf25c43b8b614fa0555ae35a7b88da5d51f47f13787d046af29d25c2bed53","event_uuid":"e1b0b988-989a-4277-992b-5b3423ab1435","position":{"commit_sha":"8d61c01900647c9e53c12f958218835ed9c722ee","position":"1787078636141737001-e1b0b988-989a-4277-992b-5b3423ab1435"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (confirmed before repair): the production snapshot contract deliberately publishes files/directories as 0444/0555 in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/snapshot.py:_chmod_readonly`. On this macOS host, an ephemeral tree with that exact shape caused plain `rm -rf` to fail with `Permission denied` on the file and `Directory not empty` on every ancestor, reproducing the original CI mechanism. Running the existing `snapshot._rmtree_writable` seam against the same residual tree removed it completely, ruling out APFS/RAM-disk specifics and proving permission restoration is sufficient. Current main applies that teardown only through `_remove_readonly_snapshot_after_test` in `tests/unit/workflow/test_snapshot.py`; symbol/caller inspection found no consumer that behaviorally depends on cleanup being module-local. The structural defect is ownership: another snapshot-producing test module can leave the identical non-removable basetemp because shared `tests/conftest.py` does not enforce the cleanup invariant. Defect legitimacy is established by the original three-run macOS failure, closed fix commit `7d908fbbc6`, and the operator requirement to repair the whole cleanup class while preserving read-only behavior. Expected post-fix behavior: snapshots remain non-writable during each test, and every `.rebar/run_snapshots` root under pytest-owned `tmp_path` is made removable during shared teardown; unrelated temp content is untouched.","timestamp":1787028129344012001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 RED checkpoint (paused before repair): signed plan-review PASS was obtained and the ticket was claimed before reproduction. The held-out cross-module subprocess oracle was collected (1 exact node), executed (not skipped/xfail), and failed for the confirmed mechanism: nested pytest exited 0 after creating a real read-only snapshot, then ordinary `shutil.rmtree` of its explicit basetemp raised `PermissionError` at the residual `.rebar/run_snapshots/<sha>` entry. This proves the test is behavioral and anti-vacuous: the producer succeeded, the snapshot was non-writable during execution, and only post-run cleanup failed. The oracle has been removed completely from the fixer worktree, the residual temp tree was cleaned through `_rmtree_writable`, and `git status --short` is clean. Frozen contract card for the blind fixer: preserve non-writable production snapshots; after shared pytest teardown, any exact `.rebar/run_snapshots` root below test-owned `tmp_path` is removable; adjacent temp content remains untouched; reuse the existing `_rmtree_writable` seam; no production/workflow behavior or dependency changes. All four collaboration slots are occupied, so no blind fixer can be spawned now. Pausing at the operator-requested RED checkpoint; no repair, gates, commit, or push has occurred.","timestamp":1787028202996688001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 final report\n\nProblem: macOS pytest basetemp cleanup failed after successful snapshot tests because read-only run_snapshots trees survived teardown.\n\nProven root cause: production snapshot publication intentionally applies 0444/0555 permissions, while cleanup was owned only by the module-local fixture in tests/unit/workflow/test_snapshot.py. Snapshot producers in any other module therefore left a non-removable .rebar/run_snapshots/<sha> below pytest basetemp. Runtime reproduction showed ordinary shutil.rmtree raising PermissionError on that exact residual tree, while snapshot._rmtree_writable removed the same tree.\n\nTest proof: tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py:22 creates a real git repository from a second module, publishes a real snapshot, and proves the file is non-writable. The nested-pytest oracle at line 46 was collected and executed, nested pytest exited 0, and the outer ordinary shutil.rmtree was legitimately RED with PermissionError at the residual .rebar/run_snapshots/<sha>. The oracle was held out from the blind fixer. Against the shared teardown it is GREEN. Exact-defect mutation removed the shared fixture and restored the old module-local-only cleanup; the final strengthened oracle returned to the same PermissionError RED after its adjacent-content assertion passed. The fix was then restored and the oracle returned GREEN.\n\nFix: tests/conftest.py:342 now owns an autouse teardown that searches only below each test-owned tmp_path for exact .rebar/run_snapshots roots and reuses snapshot._rmtree_writable. The superseded module-local fixture and unused Iterator import were removed from tests/unit/workflow/test_snapshot.py. Production snapshot permissions are unchanged.\n\nScope and safety: this restores the existing cleanup invariant at the shared pytest lifecycle boundary; it adds no production behavior, external dependency, or external call. The existing read-only assertions remain intact and no assertion was weakened. The cross-module oracle also leaves adjacent.txt beside the subject tmp_path and proves it survives shared teardown before ordinary basetemp removal, so unrelated temp content is not removed or chmodded.\n\nSibling/parity sweep: snapshot_at_ref producers were inventoried across tests/unit/workflow/test_snapshot.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_prior_art_hardening.py, and the new cross-module oracle. Prior-art hardening self-cleans in-body and remains green; the shared fixture covers current and future tmp_path-backed producers. CLI, MCP/API, public-library facade, automated runtime callers, and dual-direction parity are N/A because this is a pytest harness teardown lifecycle, not a production operation. No missing parallel surface remains.\n\nVerification: exact held-out GREEN passed; focused snapshot/cleanup/repository-isolation suite passed 30 tests; make lint passed; make typecheck passed with 555 source files; git diff --check passed. Refactoring litmus passes because the oracle asserts observable permissions, nested subprocess exit, adjacent-file preservation, and ordinary directory removal rather than fixture names or source structure.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: none observed beyond this repaired ownership seam.\n\nReplication: the original end-to-end shape now succeeds locally: nested pytest creates and validates a read-only snapshot, exits 0, shared teardown removes the exact cache root, and plain shutil.rmtree removes the explicit basetemp.","timestamp":1787030172822244001}],"created_at":1786782916770291001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"30d622f3-fa20-4625-8fad-4ec976fe9202","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5014-d0c6-5bbe-47fb"},{"link_uuid":"e3dbca0b-56d9-40a7-adfb-8f03ed1491af","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9ae7-e34e-e044-4850"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe original macOS CI incident was observed after pytest passed: owner-nonwritable `.rebar/run_snapshots` trees made ...\n## Approach\nMove the exact `.rebar/run_snapshots` teardown rule from the one snapshot test module into `tests/conftest.py`. The n...\n## Scope\n- `tests/conftest.py`: centrally remove exact run-snapshot cache roots below each test-owned `tmp_path`.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_snapshot.py`: remove the superseded module-local teardown fixture.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py`: add a snapshot-producing subject outside `test_snapshot.py` and p...\n## Testing\n- RED oracle: a subject test in `test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py` creates a real git repo under `tmp_path`, calls...\n- GREEN parity: parameterize the same nested behavior oracle over `test_snapshot.py::test_snapshot_is_read_only` and ...\n- Negative boundary: both subject tests observe read-only production snapshots before teardown. The shared fixture ta...\n- Run focused snapshot/cleanup and repository-isolation tests, then `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Nested pytest exits 0 for the snapshot-module subject; verified by `test_completed_snapshot_test_leaves_basetem...\n- [x] The snapshot-module nested basetemp is removable with ordinary `shutil.rmtree`; verified by the same test.\n- [x] Nested pytest exits 0 for the cross-module subject; verified by `test_completed_snapshot_test_leaves_basetemp_r...\n- [x] The cross-module nested basetemp is removable with ordinary `shutil.rmtree`; verified by the same test.\n- [x] Production snapshots remain non-writable before teardown; verified by `test_snapshot_is_read_only` and `test_cr...\n- [x] Cleanup removes only `.rebar/run_snapshots` roots below `tmp_path`; verified by a focused negative-boundary tes...\n- [x] The held-out oracle is RED before repair, GREEN afterward, and RED again when the old module-local-only cleanup...\n- [x] Focused tests pass.\n- [x] `make lint` passes.\n- [x] `make typecheck` passes.\n[full output: \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/rtk/tee/1787078635_jq_-r__description.log\"]","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"centralize exact run_snapshots cleanup for all tmp_path-backed tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_snapshot.py","reason":"remove superseded module-local teardown fixture"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py","reason":"prove basetemp removability across snapshot-producing test modules"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9ae7-e34e-e044-4850"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b277ede6-addf-46d5-93d5-b77b8bfbebcc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b5e6-a289-e51b-41b2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"macOS Verified-gate cleanup step fails on read-only run_snapshots dirs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["33dbdb60-f18a-455d-a2bf-c1a9166fdd24","bdadf204-b1eb-4bb2-8f7a-ad279325a822","95ebaecc-bff8-43ec-b73c-4ba120d7f7f9","4384150e-78b7-4ad9-b823-85d6ee1f84f0","b277ede6-addf-46d5-93d5-b77b8bfbebcc","f7d21b56-829c-4c27-be73-85d6ff66bbf6","dd694c38-83e0-4402-b8bb-7acd78621149","004b2e74-9ab5-414a-a37e-341212500758","990f1dc7-ce23-46c9-a8db-58973fac7cfe","e3dbca0b-56d9-40a7-adfb-8f03ed1491af","e1b0b988-989a-4277-992b-5b3423ab1435"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787078636141737002,"uuid":"f15338dc-768f-47da-a103-c5fc1e56a3be"}